 ## Overview
-Nonstandard 2D Wavelet Decomposition is a multi-dimensional extension strategy for wavelet transforms that alternates 1D transforms between rows and columns at each resolution level [S1, unofficial]. It solves the problem of mixed-resolution basis functions found in standard decompositions, providing direct control over the resolution level $m$ and ensuring all basis functions have square support [S1, unofficial]. It is more computationally efficient than the standard row-then-column approach [S1, unofficial].
+Nonstandard 2D Wavelet Decomposition is a multi-dimensional extension strategy for wavelet transforms where 1D transforms are alternated between rows and columns at each resolution level [S1, unofficial]. It solves the problem of mixed-resolution basis functions found in standard decomposition, providing direct control of the resolution level $m$ and ensuring all basis functions have square support [S1, unofficial]. It is more computationally efficient than the standard row-then-column approach [S1, unofficial].
 
